From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jayweihung <3034830+jayweihung@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:34:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] feat: a drag can refuse some drop targets

on_drag(payload, label, refuse, refused_label): refuse names the drop
targets (a target's drop_key) that won't take the drag, one per line.
Over one of them the target dims instead of its drag_over style, the
chip says refused_label, the pointer shows the not-allowed sign, and a
drop there isn't handed to the script. The agents and spaces panels key
a space's row by its id.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
